  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><mtext>and</mtext><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> be two sets containing seven and three distinct elements respectively. Then the total number of functions <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> that are onto, if there exist exactly three elements <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> such that <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pNwhw",
